@* SegmentedControl's Overview, written by hand after Button's, Card's and MultiSelect's: icons,
   full width with a hidden label, and sizes and states. It posts like a RadioGroup, whose page
   covers options from a list. Accessibility and See also come from the doc comment. *@

<Heading Level="2">Usage</Heading>
<Code Block Language="razor">@Usage</Code>
<TextBlock>A SegmentedControl is a <Anchor Href="docs/components/radio-group">RadioGroup</Anchor> shown as joined buttons. It posts the same way and works with <Anchor Href="docs/common/render-modes">JavaScript off</Anchor>. Use it for two to five short options.</TextBlock>
<TextBlock>For more options, or longer ones, use a radio group or a <Anchor Href="docs/components/select">Select</Anchor>. To switch between panels of content, use <Anchor Href="docs/components/tabs">Tabs</Anchor>.</TextBlock>
<TextBlock>A form post can carry a value that isn't among the options, so check it on the server; see <Anchor Href="docs/common/forms#values-a-form-post-can-change">Values a form post can change</Anchor>.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Icons</Heading>
<TextBlock>To put an icon before each option's text, set <Code>ItemIcon</Code>. To show only the icons, set <Code>IconOnly</Code> too.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="segmented-control-icons" />

<Heading Level="2">Full width, no visible label</Heading>
<TextBlock>To share the width equally between the segments, set <Code>FullWidth</Code>. When something near the control, such as a heading, already says what it's for, set <Code>HideLabel</Code>.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="segmented-control-full-width" />

<Heading Level="2">Sizes and disabled</Heading>
<TextBlock>To line the control up with buttons and other fields, set <Code>Size</Code>. For a choice the user can't change, set <Code>Disabled</Code>; a disabled control doesn't post.</TextBlock>
<TextBlock>There's no <Code>ReadOnly</Code>, because HTML has no read-only radio. In a read-only <Anchor Href="docs/components/form">Form</Anchor>, the control is disabled, and a hidden field posts its value.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="segmented-control-sizes" />
<TextBlock>Before saving a disabled value from a form post, see <Anchor Href="docs/common/forms#disabled-fields-and-form-posts">Disabled fields and form posts</Anchor>.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Mode support</Heading>
<ModeSupportTable Component="Component" ApiComponent="ApiComponent" />

@if (ApiComponent.Accessibility is not null)
{
    <Heading Level="2">Accessibility</Heading>
    <DocHtml Html="@ApiComponent.Accessibility" Context="@(Context with { Overview = true })" Size="ProseSize.Md" />
}

<Heading Level="2">Parameters</Heading>
<ParameterTable ApiComponent="ApiComponent" ApiHref="@Registry.ApiPageHref(Component)" Context="Context" Compact />

<OverviewSeeAlso Component="Component" ApiComponent="ApiComponent" />

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public RegistryComponent Component { get; set; } = null!;

    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public ApiComponent ApiComponent { get; set; } = null!;

    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public ApiPageContext Context { get; set; } = null!;

    private const string Usage = """
        @* An enum: each value is a segment, named by its [Display(Name)]. *@
        <SegmentedControl @bind-Value="Model!.View" />

        @* Icons only. *@
        <SegmentedControl @bind-Value="Model!.Align" ItemIcon="AlignIcon" IconOnly />

        @* Other values, with ItemText for each one's text. *@
        <SegmentedControl @bind-Value="Model!.Range" Items="Ranges.Keys" ItemText="key => Ranges[key]" />
        """;
}
